% lps-converted-from: citizenship_time.lps
% This document was written from the LPS program citizenship_time.lps, which says the same thing in the older syntax. The two run alike, and tools/lps_to_le_test.pl checks that they do. The first line above is what keeps the older file from being read as this document's companion, which would run every rule twice.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 12.

the events are:
    *a thing* borns *a second thing* with *a third thing*; known as born.
    *a thing* settles.
    *a thing* naturalises.
    *a thing* renounces.
    *a thing* birthdays; known as birthday.

the actions are:
    *a thing* registers; known as register.
    *a thing* records; known as record.

the fluents are:
    the citizen is *a thing*; known as citizen.
    *a thing* is settled; known as settled.
    *a thing* is the born in *a second thing*; known as born_in.
    *a thing* is parent *a second thing*; known as parent.
    the age of *a thing* is *a second thing*; known as age.

the knowledge base citizenship_time includes:

initially mary is settled
    and the citizen is mary.

when a thing borns a second thing with a third thing
then the thing is the born in the second thing.

when a thing borns a second thing with a third thing
then the third thing is parent the thing.

when a thing borns a second thing with a third thing
then the age of the thing is 0.

when a thing settles
then the thing is settled.

when a thing naturalises
then the citizen is the thing.

when a thing renounces
then it is not the case that the citizen is the thing.

when a thing birthdays
then the age of the thing that is a second thing becomes second thing + 1.

when a thing borns uk with a second thing
    and the citizen is the second thing
then the citizen is the thing.

when a thing borns uk with a second thing
    and the second thing is settled
then the citizen is the thing.

if a thing is the born in uk
    and it is not the case that the citizen is the thing
    and the age of the thing is a second thing
    and the second thing >= 1
then the thing registers.

when a thing registers
then the citizen is the thing.


scenario one is:
    john borns uk with mary from 2 to 3.
    pat borns uk with stranger from 3 to 4.
    pat birthdays from 5 to 6.
